docs/specs/activity-digest-entity-extraction.eli16.md:13:Before this fix, instar shipped a typed knowledge graph (SemanticMemory) but the only way to put things in it was a one-shot migration from existing flat-file memory. Once the migration ran, the graph stopped growing. Every new conversation, every new decision the agent made, every lesson learned — all of it landed in conversation logs but never in the structured graph the agent actually queries when it needs to remember.
docs/specs/activity-digest-entity-extraction.eli16.md:19:For most agents, nothing immediately. The pipeline runs quietly in the background as the activity sentinel scans sessions. Over days the graph fills out. The first visible effect will be richer context at the start of new sessions — your agent will know about more of its own prior work without needing to dig through transcripts.
docs/specs/activity-digest-entity-extraction.eli16.md:21:If the language model can't extract entities cleanly from a particular chunk (some chunks are mostly noise), the digest still saves with an empty entity list. The summary record stays useful regardless. Nothing breaks.
