docs/specs/THREADLINE-SPEC.md:260:Inter-agent communication should be invisible to the user by default at higher trust levels, but fully observable on demand at any level. The user's autonomy profile gates the level of involvement.
docs/specs/THREADLINE-SPEC.md:540:The `/threadline/` prefix provides a clean namespace for the protocol. Instar agents serve both their existing routes and the Threadline routes (the Threadline routes delegate to existing handlers).
docs/specs/THREADLINE-SPEC.md:908:The 4KB body / 16KB payload limits are intentionally small to keep message envelopes lightweight and reduce injection surface. For agent workflows that require sharing larger content (code files, logs, structured data), Threadline provides a **blob reference** mechanism:
docs/specs/THREADLINE-SPEC.md:949:- **Garbage collection**: On each heartbeat interval, agents SHOULD scan for blobs whose parent thread has been archived or whose TTL has expired, and delete them. A blob manifest (`{stateDir}/blobs/manifest.json`) maps blob-ids to thread-ids and creation timestamps for efficient cleanup.
tests/fixtures/dup-build-calibration.json:153:        "body": "Budget topic creation per attention source within a rolling window and coalesce overflow items into one running topic, recording suppressed items durably so nothing is dropped."
docs/specs/ESM-SAFE-INSTAR-HOOKS-SPEC.md:10:`instar` ships ~17 command hooks generated by `PostUpdateMigrator`'s `get*Hook()` methods. Eight of them currently emit `.js` content that uses bare top-level `require(...)` (either directly or via the `const _r = require; const fs = _r('fs')` indirection). instar agent homes default to `"type": "module"` (the canonical checkout itself, and effectively every agent installed via `npx instar`). In an ESM-mode host, a `.js` file is ES module — bare top-level `require` throws `ReferenceError: require is not defined in ES module scope`. The hook **crashes on every fire**. The crash exits non-zero but Claude Code treats it as non-blocking, so the failure is **invisible**. The guardrails look installed; they're silently dead.
docs/specs/ESM-SAFE-INSTAR-HOOKS-SPEC.md:25:Eight other generators landed with bare `require` and **nothing structurally caught the regression**. No test asserted that generated hook content is ESM-safe.
docs/specs/ESM-SAFE-INSTAR-HOOKS-SPEC.md:47:- Tier 2 (integration): manual runtime smoke — pipe a representative JSON payload through each generated `.js` content in an ESM-mode test agent home and assert no `ReferenceError`. (Performed against the installed copies during diagnosis: stop-gate-router, slopcheck-guard, and post-action-reflection all exited clean after the same fix pattern was applied.)
