docs/specs/cross-machine-secret-sync-spec.md:35:1. **No dispatcher handler.** `server.ts` wires mesh handlers for `capacity-report`, `session-status`, `place`, `claim`, `transfer`, `release`, `deliverMessage` — but **not** `secret-share`. An inbound `secret-share` envelope has nothing to process it.
docs/specs/cross-machine-secret-sync-spec.md:54:**Pull-on-miss (fallback) — DEFERRED to a follow-up.** The intended fallback: a machine that loads config and finds a `{ "secret": true }` placeholder with no local value issues a `secret-share` *request* to a peer, which responds with the per-recipient-encrypted set. v1 does **not** implement the request direction; the boot best-effort push + the deterministic lever cover the common "offline during provision" case (the returning machine pushes/pulls on its next provision or on an explicit `sync-now`). The request-driven pull is a clean, isolated follow-up.
