docs/specs/ws52-operator-tap-not-text.md:77:**Standard (a named clause of "Operator-Surface Quality", `docs/STANDARDS-REGISTRY.md`, per FD8):** *An operator-facing flow (dashboard or messaging) must never require the operator to paste raw or technical text — JSON, fingerprints, IDs, base64, CLI/curl commands — or follow a multi-step technical process. Operators act in taps and plain-language choices; the UI assembles any structured data from those taps. A flow that needs raw technical input is finished for an engineer, not its user — and is not done.*
