docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass20-verdict.md:56:The MEASURED clause says each guard *"declares no numeric horizon literal of its own"* and the clean line says the guards *"share one horizon definition"*. `HORIZON_LITERAL_RE` only matches a `const|let|var` whose **name contains "horizon"**. Replacing `const HORIZON_DAYS = COUNTDOWN_HORIZON_DAYS;` with `const GAP_DEADLINE_DAYS = 180; const HORIZON_DAYS = GAP_DEADLINE_DAYS;` leaves the lint printing `clean — 2 countdown guard(s) share one horizon definition`, which is then false. (The suite does red, but only incidentally — one test's string-replace target vanished.) Pass 19's prescription was implemented as literally written; the residual is that the sentence describing it is broader than the regex.
