docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass18-verdict.md:16:1. SEVERITY: major — The horizon "sweep" was never performed. lint-enforcement-gap-records.mjs still carries its own second copy of the bound, and six statements assert otherwise. Repair (b)'s stated design is one exported definition consumed by both countdown guards. Only lint-documented-only-countdown.mjs imports COUNTDOWN_HORIZON_DAYS. lint-enforcement-gap-records.mjs:276 retains const HORIZON_DAYS = 180 and imports nothing from the shared module. The commit which added the export never touched that file.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass18-verdict.md:82:It fails on two grounds. First, the generator is unbroken: both load-bearing findings live inside the pass-17 repair, and finding 1 is the third consecutive appearance of one shape — fix the instance, skip the pattern — this time inside the commit whose entire subject is sweeping patterns, asserted six times over. Second, "the remainder converted to expiry-dated named work" is not satisfied: finding 3 is a pass-3 defect recorded as corrected while live on the release note and the explainer, and tracked nowhere. A finding falsely marked closed is worse than an open one, because nothing will resurface it.
