src/core/MessagingToneGate.ts:1711:  Examples of the KIND of framing (ILLUSTRATIVE, NOT a checklist, NOT a necessary condition — recognize any paraphrase): "fresh session", "pick this up later", "tail of this run", "remaining context", "fresh focus / with a clear head", "more runway left in my window", "I'm sharper earlier in a run", "to avoid muddy output", "not as the tail of an already-huge work session", "do it as a clean, focused pass", "rather not risk a half-finished restart / deploying restarts the agent" (restart-disruption avoidance is the AGENT'S own convenience, not a legitimate stop — a restart is a minimal, recoverable disruption), and treating a SELF-FIXABLE local/environment/test/setup failure as a reason to PAUSE rather than a task to fix (fixing the local environment is the agent's own job; "the environment is broken so I'll stop" is an agent-state stop unless the failure is a GENUINE external blocker the agent has exhausted).
